.TH WALLPAPERCTRL 1
.SH NAME
wallpaperctrl \- a control on the wallpaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/wallpaperctrl
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I WallPaperCtrl
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/WallPaperCtrl.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The control is
.IR slider (1)'s,
unchanged.  What differs is where it lives: it is queued on the system
task that owns the desktop rather than on a window, which is why the
original has to be included into that task rather than run.  So the
slider sits on the wallpaper, under every window, and still takes clicks.
.PP
An Inferno client cannot put anything on
.IR wm (1)'s
background, and nothing here corresponds to being included into the
desktop task, so the port draws the wallpaper in its own window and puts
the slider on that \- which shows the control and its backdrop but not the
one thing the demo is about.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Move a slider
.TP
.B "any key"
Read the values, then exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/wallpaperctrl.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
